+    // the BC-250. They spent two weeks behind an interlock
+    // because they showed a rare wrong gradient on the BC-250; that turned out
+    // to be the GPU clock governor's idle-floor voltage (1000 MHz at 718 mV),
+    // not the kernels and not the compiler - 66/100 sweeps bad pinned at that
+    // point, 0/900 with the voltage back at the shipped default. See
+    // OPENCL-PERF.md, Finding 3, in mxreyer/pytorch-dlprim-gfx1013.
+    // DLPRIM_WINOGRAD_BWD_PLANES=0 /
